Grass, rubble, some bushes....not much to see, really.	草地、瓦礫，還有幾叢灌木……其實沒什麼好看的。
The ghost of the Mad Monk is here, but cannot be seen, heard or felt.  He can do you no harm.	瘋僧侶的鬼魂就在此處，但看不見、聽不到，也感覺不到。他傷不了你。
There are no ghosts here.	此處並無鬼魂。
There is no body to see here.	此處並無屍首可看。
He is a stout man with powerful arms.	他是個體格壯碩、雙臂強而有力的男子。
The Monk's garb is very old, very worn and very smelly.	這僧侶的衣袍十分老舊，破爛不堪，還臭氣沖天。
You cannot see what is not here.	不在此處之物，你看不見。
The Old Ones took the club along with the Monk's body.	古代幽靈把棍棒連同僧侶的屍身一併取走了。
It is a crude but lethal weapon.	這是件粗陋卻致命的武器。
What club?	什麼棍棒？
There are no true trees on Glastonbury Tor.  There are only some common bushes.	格列斯登伯利山上並無真正的樹木，只有些尋常的灌木。
They are common bushes.	這些是尋常的灌木。
Most of the rocks on this hill are fallen from the ancient walls.	這座山丘上的石塊，多半是從古老城牆崩落下來的。
You will not hear from these spirits again.   They have taken their silver and gone elsewhere.	這些幽靈，你不會再聽見牠們的動靜了。牠們已帶著銀兩，離去他方。
You will have to find a way to appease these Old Ones, Arthur, if you are ever to leave this Tor.	亞瑟，你必須想辦法安撫這些古代幽靈，否則休想離開這座山丘。
Such beings tend to manifest in some spot where they were once worshipped.	這類存在，往往會在昔日受人祭拜之處現身。
The "Old Ones" is a name sometimes given to ancient, elemental spirits.  Often our ancestors worshipped them as gods, but they are not, though they can be powerful.	「古代幽靈」，是人們有時用來稱呼上古元素精靈的名字。我們的祖先常將牠們奉為神明祭拜，其實牠們並非神，儘管力量確實不容小覷。
The Old Ones cannot be seen unless they will it.	古代幽靈除非自願現身，否則無法被看見。
It would be more advisable to go around.  In times of danger, it is best to keep both feet on the ground.	繞道而行才是明智之舉。身處險境時，雙腳踏實在地為上策。
The confusing swish of his robes does nothing to help you.	他袍衫窸窣紛亂的聲響，對你毫無助益。
There is an eerie quality to the wind as it blows through these ruins.  Almost like voices chanting.	風穿過這片廢墟時，帶著一股詭異的氣息，幾乎像是有人在低聲吟唱。
You will get it the hard way if you do not defend yourself!	你若不自我防衛，就準備吃苦頭吧！
Why should you want a club?  You have Excaliber.	你何必要棍棒？你已擁有聖劍。
He no longer exists on this earth.	他已不在人世。
He is not even here.	他根本不在此處。
Do something, Arthur, before HE gets YOU!	亞瑟，快做點什麼，別讓他搶先一步抓住你！
Frankly, I think you would be better off without him.	老實說，我認為沒有他，你反倒更好過。
Personally, I would touch the Monk's garb as little as possible.	依我看，那僧袍你還是少碰為妙。
You should feel no need for anything as common as a rock when you have Excaliber and your shield.	你既有聖劍與盾牌在身，何須用得著石頭這種尋常之物。
You already have it.	你已經擁有此物。
Key? What key?	鑰匙？什麼鑰匙？
You must know something I do not know.	你必定知道些我所不知道的事。
Only they can tell you what will appease them.	唯有牠們自己，才能告訴你如何安撫牠們。
Merely possessing the crystal heart has broken the Spell of Circular Entrapment that has kept you trapped upon this Tor.	光是持有水晶心，便已破除了那困你於此山丘的循環禁錮咒。
But it is an object of great power.  Keep it safe.	但此物力量非凡，務必妥善保管。
You waste your time. The monk truly IS mad!	你這是在浪費時間。這僧侶當真是瘋了！
A lot of good that will do you.	那對你毫無用處。
He is too busy ranting and raving to talk to you.	他忙著胡言亂語、瘋狂咆哮，無暇搭理你。
There is no monk here.	此處並無僧侶。
I do not think the Monk cares very much who you are.	我看這僧侶根本不在乎你是誰。
He is a pungent fellow.	他身上的氣味相當刺鼻。
The Tor smells of crushed grass and misty air.	這座山丘瀰漫著碎草與霧氣的氣息。
The well is elsewhere on the Tor.	水井在這座山丘的另一處。
There is nothing left to search.	已無他物可供搜尋。
It would help to find the monk first.	你若先找到這僧侶，會有幫助。
You will never be able to do that while he is alive, I fear.	恐怕只要他還活著，你便永遠辦不到此事。
What can you hope to hear from a madman?  But you may try it when you find him.	從一個瘋子口中，你還能指望聽到什麼？不過待你找到他，倒不妨一試。
But there is no Monk here.	但此處並無僧侶。
He has nothing to say now that he is dead.  Just as well.  His conversation was a bit limited.	他已死，如今再無話可說。也好，反正他的談吐本就乏善可陳。
Kill! Kill! Kill!	殺！殺！殺！
The dead have no use for money.	死人用不著錢財。
He does not want money.  He wants your life.	他要的不是錢財，是你的性命。
You must keep your money.  I have taken a monk's vows of poverty.	你的錢財還是自己留著吧，我已立下僧侶的清貧誓言。
Come, come.  Have a drink.	來吧，來吧，喝一杯。
Why do you hesitate?  Trust me in all things.	你何必猶豫？凡事都該信任我。
So, you will not drink, foreign dog?	這麼說，你這外邦野狗，不肯喝這一杯？
There is but one explanation for this unnatural siege of winter upon the lake -- the mood of the Lady of the Lake has turned cold, and her power affects all that is around her.	這湖泊反常地陷入寒冬圍困，只有一個解釋——湖中女神的心境轉冷，而她的力量牽動著周遭的一切。
Though the Lady now has her heart and has turned once more to warmth and the natural seasons, it will take some time for the deep cold she laid upon this lake to pass away.	雖然女神已尋回她的心，重新轉向溫暖，回歸自然時序，但她加諸於此湖的深沉寒意，仍需一段時日才能消退。
There would be no purpose in that.	那麼做並無意義。
She is beyond your voice, Arthur.	亞瑟，她聽不見你的呼喚。
All is quiet here, as though nature itself is frozen into silence.	此處萬籟俱寂，彷彿連大自然本身都凍結於沉默之中。
The glare and sparkle of the ice dazzles your eyes.	冰面的耀眼光芒與閃爍令你目眩。
No such thing can be seen.	未見此物。
A glittering palace of ice rises from the center of the lake.	一座晶瑩剔透的冰宮，自湖心聳然而立。
The heart glows with colour as power flows through it.  Study it carefully.	力量流轉其中時，這顆心便綻放出色澤。仔細端詳它。
You are surrounded by what looks like solid ice, but it could break beneath your feet at any moment.  Ridges of ice have been thrust up in places.	你周圍看似堅實的冰面，隨時都可能在你腳下裂開。有些地方的冰層被擠壓隆起成脊。
As an elemental enchantress, she can have more than one form.  In her usual watery form, she is known as the Lady of the Lake.	身為元素女巫，她能化作不只一種形貌。以她慣常的水之形貌現身時，人稱湖中女神。
And since her form usually reflects her mood, I would say that something is seriously wrong.	而她的形貌通常映照著她的心境，依我看，此刻必是出了嚴重的差錯。
He has always had the special favour of the Lady of the Lake.  Yet she is possessive and surely is not pleased with his love for Gwenhyver.	他向來深受湖中女神的特別眷顧。然而她生性佔有欲強，對他鍾情於昆海兒一事，想必極為不悅。
The lake which forms Ot Moor is frozen over.	形成奧特摩爾的這片湖水，已徹底結凍。
The spires and peaks of this cold palace have grown from the ice by the power of the Lady of the Lake.  It lies north and slightly west of the shore in the center of the lake.	這座寒冰宮殿的尖塔與峰頂，是湖中女神以其力量自冰中孕育而成，座落於湖心，偏北偏西處。
A glittering Palace made of ice has been created from the lake itself.	一座以冰築成的晶瑩宮殿，已由這片湖泊本身孕育而生。
There is naught but glaring ice and bitter cold.	此處除了刺眼的寒冰與徹骨的嚴寒，別無他物。
It is made of frozen water.  I thought you knew that.	這是凍結的水所造。我還以為你早就知曉。
It is simply ice pushed upward into a ridge by the pressure of freezing too quickly.	這不過是冰層因驟然凍結的壓力，被推擠隆起而成的一道冰脊。
The area immediately around Ot Moor is blanketed with snow, which is quite unusual, considering that it is summer.	奧特摩爾周遭一帶白雪覆蓋，時值夏季，此景著實反常。
Everything is covered with snow and ice.	萬物皆為冰雪所覆蓋。
None can be seen with all this snow and ice.	這片冰雪之中，什麼也看不見。
Aye, I sense a spell of guidance upon the rose, but it was placed there by Gwenhyver.  You must speak the Message of the Rose to invoke its spell.	正是，我感應到這朵玫瑰上有一道指引之咒，但那是昆海兒施加上去的。你必須誦念玫瑰箴言，方能喚醒此咒。
Perhaps you should consult your Liber ex Doctrina.	或許你該查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
Only the Message of the Rose can invoke the spell placed upon this flower.  Perhaps you should consult your Liber ex Doctrina.	唯有玫瑰箴言，能喚醒施加於這朵花上的咒語。或許你該查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
I have no spells to offer you, Arthur, nothing save advice.  This is your task alone.	亞瑟，我沒有咒語能給你，能給的只有忠告。此事終須你獨自承擔。
The spell is in effect! Stay within the whirlwind of petals or you will lose its protection.	咒語已然生效！留在花瓣旋風之中，否則你將失去它的護佑。
The rose trembles with the spell of the incantation, but the place is not quite right for it to work.	這朵玫瑰隨著咒語的吟誦而顫動，但此地並非它施展效力的正確場所。
It is cold as ice, clear as crystal in your hand. It pulls you toward the Ice Palace, as though eager to go within.	它在你手中冰冷如寒霜，澄澈如水晶，彷彿急欲進入冰宮一般，牽引著你朝那方向而去。
There are faint stirrings of color within the heart, flashes of golden and purple light. I sense it is caused by the nearness of the frozen lake. The ice calls to it.	這顆心之中隱隱浮動著色彩，閃現金光與紫光。我感應到這是因為靠近了這片冰封的湖泊——寒冰在召喚著它。
You ARE using it.	你正在使用它。
Fortunately, you had time on the journey here to eat, drink, rest, and don your warmer clothing as it grew colder.	所幸來此的路上，你有時間進食、飲水、歇息，並在天氣轉冷時添上禦寒的衣物。
It is so cold, your nose aches too much to smell anything.	天寒地凍，你的鼻子凍得生疼，什麼氣味都聞不出來。
Nothing here will burn.  Better to do what you must as quickly as possible and be gone.	此處無一物可燃。你該儘快辦完該辦之事，速速離去。
Across thin ice you dared to tread, 'tis no surprise that you are dead.	你竟敢踏上這薄冰之上，喪命於此，又何足詫異。
There are countless rocks in this desert.  This is yet another one.	這片沙漠裡石頭多不勝數，這不過又是其中一顆。
Aye, 'tis a rock.  A very hot rock.	正是，是顆石頭。一顆滾燙的石頭。
One rock is much like any other in this merciless terrain.	在這片無情的地域裡，石頭與石頭之間，並無太大分別。
This treacherous false guide has claimed yet another victim!  Would that you had been a bit quicker with your sword on this occasion.	這奸詐的惡嚮導，又奪走了一條性命！此番若你出劍再快一些，便不致如此。
Do not swing your sword so close to your mule, Arthur. You might hurt the poor beast.	亞瑟，別把劍舞得離你的騾子這麼近，你會傷了這可憐的畜生。
Arthur, you must find water soon or you will perish!	亞瑟，你須儘快找到水源，否則性命難保！
Your mule is suffering from lack of water!	你的騾子正因缺水而受苦！
Arthur, holding your sword constantly at the ready only serves to tire you more quickly.	亞瑟，時時刻刻持劍戒備，只會讓你更快疲憊。
Your mule suffers and needs water as urgently as you do.	你的騾子與你一樣，急需水源解渴。
You sold her to Mohammed, as you should remember.	你該記得，你已將牠賣給了穆罕默德。
There is no reason to draw your sword here.	此處沒有拔劍的理由。
That is rather difficult, since you do not have your sword.	這可有些難辦，畢竟你此刻並未佩劍。
Pay attention, Arthur. Your sword is sheathed.	亞瑟，留神些。你的劍還在鞘中。
You could, if you but had your sword.	若你佩著劍，倒是可以。
The incantation works no magick upon the rose. It awaits a time when its spell of guiding will be of the most use.	這咒語此刻對玫瑰不起作用。它等待的，是指引之咒最能派上用場的時機。
Most poetic, Arthur. And if you had Gwenhyver's rose, the incantation might even have been useful.	說得真有詩意，亞瑟。若你身上帶著昆海兒的玫瑰，這咒語或許還真能派上用場。
You are a warrior-king, not a discus thrower.	你是位征戰的王者，不是擲鐵餅的選手。
That is not how one uses a sword, as if I needed to tell you that.	劍可不是這麼用的——這種事還用得著我提醒你嗎。
The shield could be vital to your continued existence.  Which may not continue much longer with foolish notions like these.	這面盾牌，可能攸關你的存續。若總懷著這等愚蠢的念頭，你的存續怕是撐不了多久。
Life is dangerous enough without tempting fate by rampant stupidity.	人生已夠凶險，何必再以荒唐愚行去挑戰命運。
Excaliber is an extension of your very soul.  To abandon it is unthinkable.	聖劍是你靈魂的延伸，捨棄它，簡直不可思議。
What a truly mindless idea.	真是個毫無腦子的念頭。
What a foolish notion.	真是個愚蠢的念頭。
That is not only stupid, it is impossible since you do not have it.	這不僅愚蠢，而且根本不可能——你並未持有此物。
There is no need to greet me, Arthur. I am here.	亞瑟，不必向我問候，我一直都在。
This is no time to be sitting around.	此刻不是閒坐的時候。
Is that some sort of odd Gaelic word?	那是某種古怪的蓋爾語詞彙嗎？
Deeds of mindless violence will make you unworthy of the Grail.	盲目的暴行，將使你不配獲得聖杯。
This is hardly the time or place.	此時此地，都不合適。
Some other time, mayhaps.	或許改日再說吧。
There is no need for that here.	此處無需如此。
Please do.	請便。
That has gone with the mule.  A serious setback, but one which must not deter you from your mission.	那東西已隨騾子一併失去了。此乃嚴重的挫折，但不可因此讓你的使命受阻。
That is in the pack which is with the mule.....wherever she is.	那東西在騾子身上的行囊裡……不論牠此刻身在何處。
Only your deeds can determine your fate and it shall not be Merlin that renders the final judgment.	唯有你的所作所為，能決定你的命運，而最終的裁斷，也絕非出自梅林之手。
No need to thank me. My service is its own reward.	不必言謝。為你效力，本身便是回報。
Very well.	很好。
It IS a problem with armour. I am sure you will manage somehow.	甲冑一事，確實是個難題。我相信你總會設法應付過去。
The knight who wins the Grail must be pure of heart, mind, spirit and body. You seem determined to fail.	贏得聖杯的騎士，必須心、意、靈、身俱皆純淨。看來你是鐵了心要失敗。
